In the beginning, the valleys lay cracked and thirsty, their soil hard as stone. Rain fell rarely, and when it did, the water rushed away to the distant sea, leaving nothing behind.

High in the mountains lived the Ice Guardians, ancient spirits who held the winter's water frozen in their crystal palaces. Kaia, the youngest guardian, watched the struggling valleys below with growing concern.

"Why do you hoard the water?" asked a withered tree one spring.

"Because once released, it flows away forever," Kaia answered. "How can I trust it will return?"

The tree whispered, "Trust is not about return—it is about transformation. What you give freely changes the world."

